आद्यन्तवन्त: कौन्तेय न तेषु रमते बुध: ॥ २२ ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":1694,\"bb\":1497,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/22/b1497/\",\"body_value\":\"ye hi saṁsparśa-jā bhogā
duḥkha-yonaya eva te
ādy-antavantaḥ kaunteya
na teṣu ramate budhaḥ\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":1695,\"bb\":1498,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/22/b1498/\",\"shadow_value\":\"ye – those; hi – certainly; saṁsparśa-jāḥ – by contact with the material senses; bhogāḥ – enjoyments; duḥkha – distress; yonayaḥ – sources of; eva – certainly; te – they are; ādi – beginning; anta – end; vantaḥ – subject to; kaunteya – O son of Kuntī; na – never; teṣu – in those; ramate – takes delight; budhaḥ – the intelligent person.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"ye\",\"translation\":\"those\"},{\"word\":\"hi\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"saṁsparśa-jāḥ\",\"translation\":\"by contact with the material senses\"},{\"word\":\"bhogāḥ\",\"translation\":\"enjoyments\"},{\"word\":\"duḥkha\",\"translation\":\"distress\"},{\"word\":\"yonayaḥ\",\"translation\":\"sources of\"},{\"word\":\"eva\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"te\",\"translation\":\"they are\"},{\"word\":\"ādi\",\"translation\":\"beginning\"},{\"word\":\"anta\",\"translation\":\"end\"},{\"word\":\"vantaḥ\",\"translation\":\"subject to\"},{\"word\":\"kaunteya\",\"translation\":\"O son of Kuntī\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"teṣu\",\"translation\":\"in those\"},{\"word\":\"ramate\",\"translation\":\"takes delight\"},{\"word\":\"budhaḥ\",\"translation\":\"the intelligent person\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":1696,\"bb\":1499,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/22/b1499/\",\"body_value\":\"An intelligent person does not take part in the sources of misery, which are due to contact with the material senses. O son of Kuntī, such pleasures have a beginning and an end, and so the wise man does not delight in them.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1697,\"bb\":1500,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/22/b1500/\",\"body_value\":\"Material sense pleasures are due to the contact of the material senses, which are all temporary because the body itself is temporary. A liberated soul is not interested in anything which is temporary. Knowing well the joys of transcendental pleasures, how can a liberated soul agree to enjoy false pleasure? In the Padma Purāṇa it is said:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":1698,\"bb\":1501,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/22/b1501/\",\"body_value\":\"ramante yogino ’nante
satyānande cid-ātmani
iti rāma-padenāsau
paraṁ brahmābhidhīyate\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1699,\"bb\":1502,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/22/b1502/\",\"body_value\":\"“The mystics derive unlimited transcendental pleasures from the Absolute Truth, and therefore the Supreme Absolute Truth, the Personality of Godhead, is also known as Rāma.”\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1700,\"bb\":1503,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/22/b1503/\",\"body_value\":\"In the Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam also (5.5.1) it is said:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":1701,\"bb\":1504,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/5/22/b1504/\",\"body_value\":\"nāyaṁ deho deha-bhājāṁ nṛ-loke
kaṣṭān kāmān arhate viḍ-bhujāṁ ye
